1
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:29,988
-All good?
-Checks are complete.

2
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:53,970
IMMIGRATION OFFICER (MINISTRY OF JUSTICE)
KEIICHIRO HAYAMI

3
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:58,600
CUSTOMS OFFICER (MINISTRY OF FINANCE)
ATSUSHI MATSUYAMA

4
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:03,146
Creatine, approved. Zinc, approved.

5
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:05,982
Melatonin, requires confirmation.

6
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:09,069
Glutamine, approved,
assuming it matches the label.

7
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:12,739
They're just regular supplements!
There's nothing suspicious here!

8
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,700
In Japan, these are
pharmaceutical products,

9
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:17,577
not general dietary supplements.

10
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,371
They require a prescription
or fall under strict quantity limits.

11
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:22,665
Any personal supply
exceeding a two-month limit must--

12
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:24,209
Just hurry it up already!

13
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:25,168
What is she doing?

14
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:29,964
It's the rules.

15
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,217
You have a lot of these pills as well.

16
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,761
There are barely any!

17
00:01:35,887 --> 00:01:39,432
Foreign visitors in Japan have more
than doubled over the last ten years.

18
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:42,227
Over 40 million visited last year.

19
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,854
<i>We are, however,</i>
<i>nearing our limit at the front lines.</i>

20
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,981
<i>The problem lies</i>
<i>with the airport's structure itself.</i>

21
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:50,527
Immigration is handled
by the Ministry of Justice,

22
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,278
Customs by the Ministry of Finance,

23
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:55,031
Quarantine by the Ministry of Health,

24
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:58,034
and the airport police by the National
Police Agency. Furthermore,

25
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:00,745
there is the Ministry of Land,
the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

26
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:01,955
the Ministry of Defense,

27
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:03,498
the Digital Agency…

28
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:06,543
Airports are often called
a melting pot of races,

29
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:08,545
but they are also a melting pot
of government offices.

30
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:09,462
MIDORI SUGIHARA
COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM

31
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:11,506
Information is split vertically,

32
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,883
<i>and the front lines</i>
<i>are always one step behind.</i>

33
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:20,140
CHIKA KUMAGAWA - GROUND STAFF

34
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:23,017
-Yes, this way.
-Please, forward.

35
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:24,144
Hello!

36
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:44,581
Flight 2 has arrived.
Guiding 57 passengers now.

37
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:49,711
To break down these vertical walls,
a special unit led by me

38
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:51,129
that transcends the boundaries

39
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:52,881
between ministries and agencies
will begin operation.

40
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:54,883
<i>That operation is…</i>

41
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,436
Don't say it like it's an afterthought.

42
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:29,560
Mori? What are you doing?

43
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:33,648
Well, this part got dirty.

44
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:38,528
We have to take good care of our things.

45
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:58,965
-She touched it…
-What, is that bad?

46
00:04:59,048 --> 00:05:01,342
We only handle them
during basic inspections.

47
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,594
If anything happens, it leads to trouble.

48
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:34,459
Did you do this?

49
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,544
No…

50
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:48,056
What are you going to do about it?

51
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:52,060
Um, no, it wasn't me, uh…

52
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,269
Oh, come on…

53
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:56,355
Excuse me, ma'am.
Did something happen to your luggage?

54
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:59,692
My suitcase has been crushed.

55
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:02,278
I'll take care of this.

56
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:03,821
Thank you.

57
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:08,159
-This way, please.
-Go ahead.

58
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:11,579
-I'll take a look at your passport.
-Of course.

59
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:23,007
IMMIGRATION PASSPORT READING SYSTEM

60
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:27,929
2026, MARCH 22 - QUESTIONED AT HONG KONG

61
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,180
NOT DENIED ENTRY

62
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:33,101
-What did you come to Japan for?
-Just sightseeing.

63
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:34,560
How long will you stay for?

64
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,020
About five days.

65
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,649
Could you look at his luggage?

66
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,567
This way.

67
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:43,194
Huh?

68
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:46,572
Please open that man's luggage.

69
00:06:47,698 --> 00:06:48,991
Is something suspicious about him?

70
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:52,537
I can't share details.
It's Immigration Intelligence.

71
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:56,582
Just open it up.
That's all I need you to do.

72
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:59,669
No, Customs makes its own determinations.

73
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:01,838
What are you trying to check for?

74
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:06,801
Immigration exams people.
Customs exams items.

75
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,511
Let's keep to our own domains.

76
00:07:09,178 --> 00:07:11,681
Give me a reason.
I can't open it otherwise.

77
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:15,685
I am a professional at reading people.

78
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,856
-Is that seriously your reason?
-Yes.

79
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:22,233
What is this?

80
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,445
Don't be so arrogant,
Mr. Immigration Agent.

81
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:26,571
I am Hayami.

82
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,158
Customs officers are so hard-headed.

83
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:32,660
My name's Matsuyama!

84
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:38,583
What's wrong?

85
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:40,710
Chief Officer…

86
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,378
Excuse me…

87
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:46,799
-May I inspect this luggage?
-Hey, what do you think you're doing?

88
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:49,802
Fine.

89
00:07:56,934 --> 00:07:59,145
This suitcase is heavy.

90
00:07:59,228 --> 00:08:01,063
-Heavy?
-Yes.

91
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:03,691
Especially near the bottom.

92
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:06,110
Enough to crush the bag
that was underneath it.

93
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,070
Is there something heavy inside?

94
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:11,407
-The scale is there.
-Most likely the wheels.

95
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,660
These wheels are strange.

96
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:19,582
The wheels on all the other suitcases
were warm from the outside temperature,

97
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:24,170
but these wheels are as cool
as the air-conditioned room.

98
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:25,588
Meaning?

99
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:28,424
The material of these wheels isn't rubber.

100
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,719
It's a heavy metal with high thermal
conductivity and high specific gravity.

101
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:33,137
In other words, it's basically--

102
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:34,931
Don't touch that!

103
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:53,199
Whoa, whoa, whoa…

104
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:05,294
Oh my…

105
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:09,131
BORDER CONTROL

106
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:11,801
<i>This morning</i>
<i>at Kanto International Airport,</i>

107
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:14,345
<i>the Metropolitan Police Department</i>
<i>arrested</i>

108
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,430
<i>a foreign national on suspicion</i>

109
00:09:16,514 --> 00:09:18,599
<i>of attempting to smuggle gold bullion…</i>

110
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:21,394
Why are the police getting all the credit?

111
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:24,772
Gate 24 wasn't mentioned even once!

112
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,024
Counselor Sugihara.

113
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:29,986
Congratulations on the launch
of the new unit.

114
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,153
Airport Director Ikeura.

115
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,071
TAKAHIRO IKEURA
DIRECTOR OF KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

116
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:33,447
Breaking down the walls
between ministries and agencies.

117
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:35,700
A truly admirable concept.

118
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:40,705
However, as someone responsible
for running the airport,

119
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,623
I have been hearing some concerns.

120
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,166
Concerns?

121
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,043
When there's a problem,

122
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:49,380
who makes the decision,
and who takes the blame?

123
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:52,717
You need to make that clear.

124
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,344
Those of us on the ground

125
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:58,389
can't operate on ideals alone, you know.

126
00:09:58,889 --> 00:09:59,890
Good day.

127
00:10:12,069 --> 00:10:14,280
It doesn't seem like
all the ministries and agencies

128
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:16,991
are being very cooperative.

129
00:10:17,074 --> 00:10:20,703
Everyone cares more about
their own turf than the country.

130
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:26,584
And the location is practically
a deserted island too.

131
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:27,710
Yes.

132
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:31,464
For now, it's a six-month trial operation,

133
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,383
handling mostly temporary
and charter flights.

134
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:37,011
<i>Basically, we're being treated</i>
<i>as benchwarmers.</i>

135
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:38,262
<i>Benchwarmers, huh?</i>

136
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:39,639
I suppose I am

137
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:43,351
an old hearing officer
nearing retirement myself.

138
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,895
You're Chief Hearing Officer.

139
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:49,315
Having you on board, Fukasawa,

140
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:51,525
gives me so much reassurance.

141
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:52,860
I'm honored.

142
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,321
Besides,

143
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:58,658
I actually like this team.

144
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:03,913
I heard it was a motley crew thrown
together from various departments,

145
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:07,333
but they seem like
quite an interesting group.

146
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:12,338
The next flight will be
the last one handled by Gate 24 today.

147
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,715
Ah, I'm exhausted…

148
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:17,843
I've been moving since the morning.
My feet have hit their limit.

149
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,804
My bangs have hit their limit too.

150
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,599
Everyone, just one last push.

151
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,061
Matsuyama, are you listening?

152
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,687
Did you see this?

153
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:30,606
Only 500 views.

154
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:34,735
Gate 24… It isn't
being talked about at all.

155
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:38,697
Excuse me, customs officer, personal web
browsing during work hours isn't allowed…

156
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:41,909
Aren't you guys in Immigration
and Quarantine frustrated too?

157
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:44,078
After all the effort
to launch this new unit…

158
00:11:44,161 --> 00:11:45,413
But isn't the general public

159
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:49,041
pretty uninterested in Immigration,
Customs, and Quarantine anyway?

160
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:51,293
I feel like people
don't even know the difference.

161
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:54,922
It is not something
we should concern ourselves with.

162
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:58,384
Let through those who should be
and stop those who should not be.

163
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:00,594
That is all we need to do.

164
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:01,971
Exactly!

165
00:12:02,471 --> 00:12:05,224
That is the exact mission
entrusted to Gate 24.

166
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:07,393
As expected of the Ministry of Justice!

167
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:09,437
As expected of a career official!

168
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:14,400
Is that guy a career official?

169
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,777
They say he's a future candidate
for management,

170
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:19,113
but he volunteered because he wanted
to work on the front lines,

171
00:12:19,196 --> 00:12:21,574
and he went through
proper training before coming here.

172
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,117
Why go out of his way to do that?

173
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,953
Because if you don't know the front lines,
you can't design system policies.

174
00:12:26,036 --> 00:12:27,705
Wonderful!

175
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,458
Those words are practically
the constitution!

176
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:34,336
Still, it's a problem
to only focus on people.

177
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,465
Over here, we have to look at the goods.

178
00:12:38,174 --> 00:12:40,509
Danger isn't necessarily limited
to people, after all.

179
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:50,686
By the way, what's she about?

180
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:52,521
Well, I don't really know either.

181
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:56,275
I usually hear about most things,

182
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:58,402
but regarding that girl,
I've got zero information.

183
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,529
She just keeps wiping things down.

184
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:02,531
Mori.

185
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,242
Machi Mori.

186
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:09,413
Yes?

187
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:12,791
Where was your previous
field assignment, Mori?

188
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,627
Field assignment…

189
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:20,216
This is my first time.

190
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:27,306
<i>Announcement for passengers.</i>

191
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:29,934
<i>Southeast Asia Airlines Flight 226</i>

192
00:13:30,017 --> 00:13:33,103
<i>from Ho Chi Minh City</i>
<i>will arrive at Gate 24.</i>

193
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,191
We'll take our luggage. Please proceed.

194
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:41,070
There are two booths.
Please proceed in the line.

195
00:13:47,576 --> 00:13:50,162
What does she mean this is her first time?

196
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:53,499
I doubt she's a complete rookie, though.

197
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:56,835
She's wiping things again…

198
00:14:05,844 --> 00:14:07,805
Passports, please.

199
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,358
Please take your luggage over here.

200
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,237
-Is this all your luggage?
-Yes.

201
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,739
-Do you have anything to declare?
-No.

202
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:26,699
That's all right.

203
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:30,327
Are you traveling?

204
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:34,123
-It's our honeymoon. Honeymoon.
-Yes.

205
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:36,500
My wife comes to Japan a lot.
She loves it here, so…

206
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:38,419
I can see that.

207
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,724
How long do you plan to stay?

208
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:53,350
Two weeks.

209
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,483
Please step this way and use this booth.

210
00:15:02,484 --> 00:15:04,695
Could I have a moment with both of you?

211
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:10,576
-Please take their luggage.
-Okay.

212
00:15:11,118 --> 00:15:11,952
This way.

213
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:23,380
Please, have a seat.

214
00:15:24,548 --> 00:15:26,967
Why… Why did you bring us here?

215
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:28,844
It's just a formal check.

216
00:15:32,681 --> 00:15:35,184
Excuse me. What do I do with this luggage?

217
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:36,518
Keep it with the passengers.

218
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:39,605
Please wait here a moment.

219
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,698
Did something happen again?

220
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:52,493
Hayami!

221
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:55,537
-Seike, what about the inspections?
-I had Natori take over for me?

222
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,041
Um…

223
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,044
I saw you do this earlier.

224
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:05,339
What is that?

225
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:09,510
That's a hand signal
we've established in Immigration.

226
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:10,719
It's a signal for a suspicious person.

227
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:13,305
I see. A hand signal…

228
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:19,019
So those two really are suspicious, right?

229
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:22,773
-Just tell me already.
-I said, this is Immigration Intelligence.

230
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:24,775
Excuse me…

231
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:28,487
<i>To break down these vertical walls,</i>

232
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:30,864
-What are you doing?
-<i>starting today, a special unit led by me</i>

233
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:32,324
that transcends the boundaries

234
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:34,618
between ministries and agencies
will begin operation.

235
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:37,413
That is what she said.

236
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:42,167
So, in other words, at Gate 24,
we share information,

237
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,085
right?

238
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:45,254
That's…

239
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:49,591
Yes. I was so happy about the whole thing,
I rewatched it many times.

240
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:52,720
These are the words
of Counselor Midori Sugihara

241
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:54,972
from the Cabinet Secretariat
Border Control Reform Office.

242
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:56,348
<i>Gate 24</i>

243
00:16:57,182 --> 00:16:59,101
<i>is a brand new system, so…</i>

244
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:01,353
Indeed… Hayami.

245
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:04,148
-We should work as a team and share--
-Provided that

246
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:06,316
nothing leaks to the outside.

247
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:08,694
Of course.

248
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,488
You too.

249
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:14,908
Yes. Information is shared.
Confidentiality is strict.

250
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:22,708
Regarding that couple,
the husband is Samir Sadikov.

251
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:23,959
The wife is Lylea Sadikova.

252
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:26,670
Both are from the Zafaria Federation.

253
00:17:27,629 --> 00:17:29,965
Before coming to Japan,
they stopped in Vietnam,

254
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,760
but they were refused entry
during local inspections.

255
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:34,053
I see.

256
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:39,475
The Counselor is here right now as well.
Let's listen to this together.

257
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:42,394
Excuse me.

258
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:49,151
Did you run an inquiry on that couple?

259
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:50,694
Yes, however,

260
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:52,571
the current situation
in Zafaria is unstable,

261
00:17:52,654 --> 00:17:54,740
so we cannot make inquiries
with their local authorities,

262
00:17:54,823 --> 00:17:56,992
and we haven't been able
to verify their identities yet.

263
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:57,993
I see.

264
00:17:58,077 --> 00:17:59,787
Until things are clear,

265
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:03,832
we should consider having them wait
without permitting entry.

266
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,168
-<i>Yes, sir.</i>
-Hayami.

267
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:08,587
I'll leave the questioning
of those two to you.

268
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:12,966
-Understood.
<i>-This is perfect.</i>

269
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:16,887
Why not have Customs lend a hand as well?

270
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:19,389
Counselor Sugihara…

271
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:21,475
Customs as well?

272
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:23,685
<i>There are things that can be seen</i>
<i>through the goods, aren't there?</i>

273
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,772
Shall we give it a try?

274
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,191
<i>This might be</i>

275
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:33,278
an excellent opportunity
to demonstrate the value of Gate 24.

276
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,323
I want Immigration and Customs
to work together to find the answer

277
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:39,535
as to whether those two
should be allowed entry or not.

278
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:41,829
Yes, leave it to us.

279
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,297
Apologies for keeping you waiting.

280
00:18:53,048 --> 00:18:55,634
What's going on? Can we go?

281
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:58,345
To help with that,
please let us ask a few questions.

282
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:05,769
Before coming to Japan,
you two were refused entry in Vietnam.

283
00:19:06,645 --> 00:19:08,188
We don't know.

284
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:09,690
You don't know?

285
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:13,819
Because they didn't tell us.

286
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:14,945
I see.

287
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:20,033
May we check the contents of this luggage?

288
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,452
Here? You go through luggage here?

289
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:26,165
Of course, it's voluntary,
but if you cooperate,

290
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:27,249
the check will be finished quickly.

291
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:31,211
Okay, okay. I open.

292
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:49,605
-Are you okay?
-Get the first aid kit.

293
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:51,023
It's okay. It's fine. It's okay.

294
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:52,691
Just, please, check.

295
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,443
Thank you.

296
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:56,695
To ensure there are no mix-ups
upon return,

297
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:58,864
we will record
the condition of the contents.

298
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:00,991
I'll do it.

299
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,870
Okay then.

300
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:06,788
-Please do so.
-Yes.

301
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:20,594
So the couple shares one piece of luggage…

302
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:22,638
May I ask?

303
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:28,518
You two are newlyweds,
but when and where did you meet?

304
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:30,687
It was about, uh,

305
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:33,982
about five years ago. Through a friend.

306
00:20:34,524 --> 00:20:35,817
I'm asking Lylea.

307
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:38,987
Wait, hold on…

308
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:42,574
Ah, this, yes, this. This is ours.

309
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:43,659
I'll show…

310
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,912
This is Lylea's family.

311
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:48,288
Lylea's family.

312
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,500
-Show.
-Oh, yes, um…

313
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,419
This… This is my older brother,

314
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:59,299
my parents, and my little sister.

315
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:03,095
My older brother introduced us.

316
00:21:03,845 --> 00:21:04,680
Thank you.

317
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:07,057
They look like a close-knit family.

318
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:09,768
That was from the party
we threw at our place.

319
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:26,952
Is it a pair of dolls?

320
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:28,537
Very cute.

321
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:30,956
Yes.

322
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,541
They were a wedding gift.

323
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:36,128
Could we please just get this over with?

324
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:38,630
We have a hotel reservation, so…

325
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:41,925
Then, continuing with the questions…

326
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:43,510
Hayami.

327
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:52,269
I'm Iuchi from the Metropolitan Police
Department's International Crime Division.

328
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:54,062
-Tamai.
-Hello.

329
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:56,440
-Someone's here.
-We were called here.

330
00:21:56,523 --> 00:21:57,983
Likewise, I'm Nakatsuka.

331
00:21:58,066 --> 00:21:59,067
Hello.

332
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,778
You came because of those two.
Do you know something?

333
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,156
I'll cut straight to the conclusion.

334
00:22:05,699 --> 00:22:08,827
Let those two enter.

335
00:22:10,871 --> 00:22:12,664
Why? Are those two--

336
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:13,915
We can't share details.

337
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:15,167
It's police intelligence.

338
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:19,254
Are you familiar
with the Immigration Control Act?

339
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:22,924
This decision is the duty of Immigration.

340
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:26,887
You can't suddenly ask us to grant entry
without a formal request.

341
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:30,432
Shut up. It's always
every little thing with you guys.

342
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:34,811
This matter involves
a criminal investigation.

343
00:22:35,395 --> 00:22:36,563
End of story.

344
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:40,984
You guys just need
to open and close the doors.

345
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:52,871
Wait. What do you mean?

346
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:55,082
They were refused entry in Vietnam,

347
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:56,958
but the Japanese police
are telling us to let them in?

348
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:59,336
They wouldn't tell us
the reason or anything.

349
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:02,130
Why don't we just let them in?

350
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:05,509
Setting aside the detective's attitude,

351
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:08,470
it means the police
will take responsibility.

352
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,139
As Immigration, don't we
just have to comply?

353
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:13,433
You're right! Shall we do that then?

354
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:14,935
Um…

355
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:16,728
If you talk about responsibility,

356
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:18,522
there's also the responsibility
of letting them in.

357
00:23:19,272 --> 00:23:20,315
Well, when you put it that way…

358
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:21,691
Um…

359
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:25,403
At present, the grounds for refusing entry
to those two are weak.

360
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:29,074
-I suppose so.
-That doesn't mean you can just…

361
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:29,991
Excuse me!

362
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:31,910
Um…

363
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:33,495
Wait, wait, Mori.

364
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:34,579
What are you doing?

365
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:37,707
Making my own kind of hand signal.

366
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:41,503
-Excuse me?
-I'm glad you noticed.

367
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:42,546
That was a signal just now?

368
00:23:42,629 --> 00:23:44,422
Yes. Um…

369
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,760
-Regarding these dolls…
-Dolls?

370
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:49,928
What are you talking about?

371
00:23:50,011 --> 00:23:52,931
Ah, the ones Lylea said
were a wedding gift.

372
00:23:53,014 --> 00:23:54,057
Yes.

373
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:57,352
The shape of these arms
forms a semaphore signal.

374
00:23:57,435 --> 00:23:59,062
Semaphore signal?

375
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:00,856
It's like flag signaling.

376
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:03,316
It conveys letters of the alphabet
through arm angles.

377
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:06,862
This shape is "E". And

378
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:09,614
this one is "M".

379
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:11,199
E, M?

380
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:12,659
Emergency?

381
00:24:12,742 --> 00:24:15,203
Yes. It means an emergency situation.

382
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:17,706
Wait a minute.
These dolls are saying that?

383
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:21,626
Or rather, did someone move
these dolls' arms to convey that?

384
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:23,753
I don't know.

385
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:27,215
However, I thought this might
also be some kind of sign.

386
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:29,759
Is that woman asking for help?

387
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:32,637
Well, it might just be a coincidence
that they're in this shape.

388
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:34,639
Mori, how do you even know
about these signals?

389
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:36,141
May I investigate this in more detail?

390
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:37,934
What, Mori?

391
00:24:42,439 --> 00:24:44,983
I want to investigate a bit more too.

392
00:24:45,984 --> 00:24:49,779
To me, it looked like Lylea was terrified.

393
00:24:50,655 --> 00:24:51,489
What about you, Hayami?

394
00:24:52,282 --> 00:24:53,742
Aren't you a pro at seeing through people?

395
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:56,703
What if she really

396
00:24:57,287 --> 00:24:59,247
is asking for help?

397
00:25:05,128 --> 00:25:06,838
Even if we investigate…

398
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:11,968
wouldn't it just be a waste of time?

399
00:25:12,052 --> 00:25:15,847
It doesn't matter if it's a waste, right?

400
00:25:17,349 --> 00:25:20,936
That's our job, isn't it?

401
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:35,617
Are you done yet? Huh?
Are you done yet? Yes, no?

402
00:25:35,700 --> 00:25:38,453
May we inspect your luggage one more time?

403
00:25:39,287 --> 00:25:41,790
Fine. Whatever. Fine. Okay, okay.

404
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:44,501
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

405
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:13,571
ANALYZING

406
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:18,576
This is called TDS--

407
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:20,912
It's a machine that wipes
the luggage surface

408
00:26:20,996 --> 00:26:23,081
to check for traces of drugs
or explosives.

409
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:26,418
Right?

410
00:26:29,129 --> 00:26:30,505
Did you come to help out?

411
00:26:30,588 --> 00:26:32,424
No, this is a customs officer's work.

412
00:26:32,507 --> 00:26:33,425
Did anything come up?

413
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:35,010
NOTHING FOUND

414
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:37,846
No traces of illegal substances
were detected.

415
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:39,222
A swing and a miss, then.

416
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:41,433
If you're just here to mock us,
could you leave?

417
00:26:43,059 --> 00:26:45,061
Um…

418
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:50,817
Regarding these keys…

419
00:26:52,777 --> 00:26:55,280
Each one of them has their own keys?

420
00:26:56,031 --> 00:26:56,906
What could these keys be for?

421
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:59,784
This one is for a car, maybe.

422
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:03,288
The other is a motorcycle and… a padlock?

423
00:27:04,497 --> 00:27:06,082
Then, what about this one?

424
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:09,669
A front door key? For the couple's home.

425
00:27:10,253 --> 00:27:11,796
I think so too.

426
00:27:12,380 --> 00:27:14,090
But it's strange.

427
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:17,218
That couple seems to be living
in the same home.

428
00:27:17,302 --> 00:27:19,929
In that case, shouldn't each spouse

429
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:23,266
have one front door key?

430
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:27,312
Indeed…

431
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,901
It means only one of them
has the key to the house.

432
00:27:32,984 --> 00:27:35,904
-Is that normal?
-No, it's strange.

433
00:27:37,697 --> 00:27:40,158
Are those two really a married couple?

434
00:27:41,409 --> 00:27:42,827
Hey, Hayami,

435
00:27:43,536 --> 00:27:46,331
since when do you do Customs work?

436
00:27:48,416 --> 00:27:49,292
Excuse me.

437
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,841
I'm also curious about this key.

438
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:58,426
What key could it be?

439
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:01,388
A key to a warehouse
somewhere or something?

440
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:06,476
You notice a lot of things, don't you,
Mori? Your knowledge is broad too.

441
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:08,603
What were you doing up until now?

442
00:28:14,109 --> 00:28:15,485
Are you listening?

443
00:28:15,568 --> 00:28:17,529
Oh, are you in the middle of something?

444
00:28:17,612 --> 00:28:20,281
We looked into that couple.

445
00:28:21,991 --> 00:28:25,578
Tamai reached out to all her connections
across the airport.

446
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:28,665
We were able to hear from staff
knowledgeable about international crime.

447
00:28:28,748 --> 00:28:30,208
You have acquaintances like that?

448
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:33,545
I live purely on human connections.

449
00:28:33,628 --> 00:28:36,423
Endo also looked into local news articles.

450
00:28:36,506 --> 00:28:38,842
For Quarantine, information
is life, after all. Low-key.

451
00:28:38,925 --> 00:28:40,760
And from that,
we found out that right now,

452
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:43,680
a human trafficking group from Zafaria

453
00:28:43,763 --> 00:28:45,682
is active across all of Asia.

454
00:28:45,765 --> 00:28:47,183
That organization

455
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:49,602
doesn't just target the individual,
but their entire family as well, it seems.

456
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:52,397
-The entire family?
-Then,

457
00:28:52,939 --> 00:28:54,524
those two…

458
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:57,193
Samir

459
00:28:57,277 --> 00:28:58,987
is a broker for the organization,

460
00:28:59,070 --> 00:29:00,572
and Lylea's family was taken hostage,

461
00:29:00,655 --> 00:29:02,615
and she was brought to Japan
against her will,

462
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,367
or so I presume.

463
00:29:04,451 --> 00:29:05,827
Seriously?

464
00:29:08,204 --> 00:29:11,166
But that makes everything add up.

465
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:15,795
They're a fake couple,
which is why there was only one house key.

466
00:29:15,879 --> 00:29:18,715
Plus, Lylea has been
to Japan multiple times,

467
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:21,509
so she's highly valuable to Samir.

468
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,719
For getting through
immigration inspection too.

469
00:29:22,802 --> 00:29:24,220
-That's true.
-Hey.

470
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:28,099
-What do you think?
-What are you going to do?

471
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:32,854
You're not being very clear.

472
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:37,734
In the end, Hayami, you just don't
want to take responsibility, right?

473
00:29:40,069 --> 00:29:42,489
Now, now, it's still speculation.

474
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:44,699
For now, let's report to Fukasawa.

475
00:29:48,244 --> 00:29:51,539
You haven't let them into the country yet?

476
00:29:59,088 --> 00:30:01,049
Well, yes, the police

477
00:30:01,132 --> 00:30:06,179
had also caught onto the possibility
that Samir was connected

478
00:30:06,262 --> 00:30:07,722
to a human trafficking ring.

479
00:30:09,015 --> 00:30:11,601
You wanted to let him enter
rather than arrest him here,

480
00:30:11,684 --> 00:30:12,977
to get the tail of the organization.

481
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:14,062
Was that the goal?

482
00:30:14,145 --> 00:30:16,523
So that's what's going on…

483
00:30:16,606 --> 00:30:19,984
-But we can't at least protect Lylea?
-Doing something like that

484
00:30:20,068 --> 00:30:23,488
would be as good as notifying
the target that the police suspect them.

485
00:30:23,571 --> 00:30:25,657
Well, that's true…

486
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:27,075
Hey, what even is this place?

487
00:30:28,159 --> 00:30:31,329
Are you sharing Immigration Intelligence
with Customs and Quarantine here?

488
00:30:31,412 --> 00:30:34,290
-Well, that's…
-Yes.

489
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:35,708
A special unit that transcends
the boundaries

490
00:30:35,792 --> 00:30:36,835
between ministries and agencies.

491
00:30:36,918 --> 00:30:39,462
This is Gate 24.

492
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:43,258
Right?

493
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:47,804
-Something like that's impossible.
-Right?

494
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:51,474
At any rate, hurry up the procedures.

495
00:30:51,558 --> 00:30:55,436
If the target catches wind
of the police presence, it's all over.

496
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:58,147
Can you take responsibility
if that happens?

497
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:04,404
-Understood.
-Alright.

498
00:31:04,487 --> 00:31:05,446
Hey, Hayami…

499
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:07,824
-It's a police request.
-Even so,

500
00:31:07,907 --> 00:31:09,617
Are you just going
to leave Lylea with him?

501
00:31:11,035 --> 00:31:13,121
Even though she sent a help signal?

502
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:17,041
Is Immigration fine with that?

503
00:31:20,587 --> 00:31:21,880
It's not my call.

504
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:29,762
Don't say it so lightly.

505
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:33,683
Customs can't even take responsibility,
so you should stay out of this.

506
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:40,440
Well, now, thank you, everyone,
for your hard work.

507
00:31:40,523 --> 00:31:41,566
Fukusawa…

508
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:45,945
-I am Chief Hearing Officer Fukasawa.
-Oh, hello.

509
00:31:46,029 --> 00:31:47,572
I have heard the circumstances.

510
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:52,076
The final decision regarding entry
will be made by me.

511
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:55,079
Then give the go-ahead now.

512
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:57,415
Don't be in such a rush.

513
00:31:57,498 --> 00:32:01,044
Actually, officials
from the Ministry of Justice

514
00:32:01,127 --> 00:32:05,798
and National Police Agency
are currently conferring on this matter.

515
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:07,842
Let's wait for their conclusion,

516
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:13,681
or would acting on your own in the field

517
00:32:14,182 --> 00:32:17,185
turn into a responsibility issue itself?

518
00:32:43,294 --> 00:32:44,545
What are you doing?

519
00:32:45,213 --> 00:32:46,297
Investigating.

520
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:48,174
That's enough.

521
00:32:48,675 --> 00:32:50,385
There's nothing more
the front line can do.

522
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:57,976
It's just as the police said.

523
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:01,437
A unit like this was impossible.

524
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:05,149
Immigration and Customs
are completely different.

525
00:33:06,442 --> 00:33:08,861
Customs looks at goods. If there's
something illegal, they stop it.

526
00:33:08,945 --> 00:33:10,697
If not, they let it pass.

527
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:12,615
It's black and white.

528
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:16,244
But Immigration deals with people.

529
00:33:16,327 --> 00:33:18,955
More often than not,
it can't be divided into black or white.

530
00:33:19,706 --> 00:33:22,792
So while it remains gray,
a line has to be drawn somewhere.

531
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:28,131
You should just call it quits too now.

532
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:30,508
Because this matter
is already covered in gray.

533
00:33:30,591 --> 00:33:31,968
Um…

534
00:33:36,264 --> 00:33:39,142
What color is that gray?

535
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:42,603
-Excuse me?
-Even if you say it's gray,

536
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:44,522
there are many kinds.

537
00:33:44,605 --> 00:33:47,025
Gray close to white, gray close to black.

538
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:50,278
Gray mixed with blue or red.

539
00:33:50,361 --> 00:33:52,321
There are countless types.

540
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:57,493
What color gray is this matter?

541
00:34:02,915 --> 00:34:05,752
I want to know that.

542
00:34:06,502 --> 00:34:11,924
Because I dislike leaving things
I don't understand unknown.

543
00:34:21,976 --> 00:34:23,227
This zipper…

544
00:34:25,396 --> 00:34:29,942
Look, this zipper is made
of flexible resin and is easy to close.

545
00:34:32,403 --> 00:34:33,446
What about it?

546
00:34:37,992 --> 00:34:39,077
What are you doing there?

547
00:34:40,036 --> 00:34:41,370
Counselor Sugihara…

548
00:34:43,623 --> 00:34:45,083
A conclusion has been reached.

549
00:34:45,708 --> 00:34:47,877
They say to grant entry to the two.

550
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:51,464
So we're just going
to leave Lylea with him…

551
00:34:52,131 --> 00:34:55,384
I'm worried, but I suppose
it can't be helped.

552
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:57,678
Well then, Hayami,

553
00:34:58,221 --> 00:35:00,348
could I ask you to handle
their entry procedures?

554
00:35:02,850 --> 00:35:04,477
Are you unhappy with something?

555
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:08,022
No, it's a decision from above.

556
00:35:09,565 --> 00:35:10,399
It's just

557
00:35:10,900 --> 00:35:12,318
this one thing.

558
00:35:19,242 --> 00:35:22,245
I've been bothered
by this photo the whole time.

559
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:24,413
Everyone in the family is smiling,

560
00:35:25,164 --> 00:35:27,583
but somehow, they look tense.

561
00:35:27,667 --> 00:35:28,835
Tense?

562
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,421
For instance…

563
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:36,008
-Okay, say cheese!
-<i>What if when this photo was taken,</i>

564
00:35:36,092 --> 00:35:37,677
-Okay!
-<i>Lylea</i>

565
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:40,805
<i>and her entire family</i>
<i>had already been abducted</i>

566
00:35:40,888 --> 00:35:45,059
<i>and a gun was being pointed</i>
<i>at them from behind the camera?</i>

567
00:35:46,185 --> 00:35:48,062
Even if we let those two pass like this,

568
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:51,149
I wonder if Lylea's family
will really be okay?

569
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:56,529
That said, it's just speculation.
Besides, it's too late now.

570
00:35:57,155 --> 00:35:58,197
No,

571
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:00,449
it's worth investigating.

572
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:05,496
Shall I negotiate with the top
to buy us just a little more time?

573
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:07,707
In the meantime,

574
00:36:08,457 --> 00:36:09,917
whether it's a clue about the organization

575
00:36:10,793 --> 00:36:13,504
or Lylea's family, anything goes.

576
00:36:13,588 --> 00:36:16,174
Find grounds enough to stop those two.

577
00:36:16,257 --> 00:36:18,926
-No, but, like I said, this was just--
-Let's do it.

578
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:21,262
If it comes down to responsibility,
I will take it.

579
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:24,307
Incredible…

580
00:36:24,390 --> 00:36:27,602
-So cool…
-All right, let's go, go, go.

581
00:36:34,358 --> 00:36:36,444
Apologies for keeping you waiting.

582
00:36:36,527 --> 00:36:38,613
-I am Chief Hearing Officer Fukasawa.
-What now?

583
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:41,449
How long do you plan
on keeping us for? Huh?

584
00:36:41,532 --> 00:36:42,658
I am very sorry.

585
00:36:43,326 --> 00:36:46,829
Last step. Please allow us to speak
with each of you individually.

586
00:36:47,914 --> 00:36:50,082
One by one, huh? One by one?

587
00:36:50,166 --> 00:36:52,335
Starting with yourself.

588
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:56,547
I refuse. No. No!

589
00:36:56,631 --> 00:37:01,219
If you comply,
we won't detain you any longer.

590
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:05,932
Okay, but this is it.
After, you'll let us go.

591
00:37:07,516 --> 00:37:08,684
This way, please.

592
00:37:23,491 --> 00:37:25,701
What's going on? What?

593
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:27,912
He won't be back for a while.

594
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:30,957
Could you tell me in detail
about the situation

595
00:37:31,874 --> 00:37:33,376
you are currently in?

596
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:44,387
I see. So they split the two up.

597
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:49,308
-I hope it goes well.
-It comes down to Hayami, then…

598
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:53,688
We got some time. But only 30 minutes.

599
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:54,939
That's short…

600
00:38:00,278 --> 00:38:01,195
Lylea.

601
00:38:02,363 --> 00:38:04,991
We got the message in your luggage.

602
00:38:05,741 --> 00:38:08,119
We also have a lead on that man

603
00:38:08,786 --> 00:38:10,371
and that your family

604
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:13,291
is currently in a dangerous situation.

605
00:38:15,042 --> 00:38:17,461
All we need now is to hear it from you.

606
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:21,507
Please, speak to us.

607
00:38:26,429 --> 00:38:28,431
Look, there's no time.
Let's search for evidence over here too.

608
00:38:28,514 --> 00:38:29,640
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

609
00:38:30,266 --> 00:38:32,143
You tell us to look for evidence, but…

610
00:38:32,852 --> 00:38:34,895
Don't the police have any information?

611
00:38:34,979 --> 00:38:36,689
Like the identity of the organization.

612
00:38:37,231 --> 00:38:39,275
We don't know their exact base,

613
00:38:39,358 --> 00:38:42,069
but we've narrowed it down to some extent.

614
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:43,446
Whereabouts?

615
00:38:43,529 --> 00:38:45,323
-We can't tell you that.
-That's right.

616
00:38:45,406 --> 00:38:47,325
Um…

617
00:38:47,867 --> 00:38:50,286
Is that base in Aichi Prefecture?

618
00:38:50,369 --> 00:38:51,495
That's right. What?!

619
00:38:53,247 --> 00:38:56,042
This photo is strange.

620
00:38:57,877 --> 00:39:01,255
-This tree looks like a Hananoki.
-Hananoki?

621
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,132
It's a tree unique to Japan.

622
00:39:03,215 --> 00:39:06,218
It's distributed mainly in limited areas
of the Chubu region

623
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:08,554
and is also the prefectural tree
of Aichi Prefecture.

624
00:39:08,637 --> 00:39:10,473
It shouldn't be seen in Zafaria.

625
00:39:10,556 --> 00:39:12,016
What? Then, this photo was…

626
00:39:12,099 --> 00:39:13,768
Taken in Japan?

627
00:39:13,851 --> 00:39:15,603
Excuse me a second here.

628
00:39:16,145 --> 00:39:17,355
Then what about this utility pole?

629
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:19,940
Doesn't it provide some clue?

630
00:39:20,608 --> 00:39:22,193
I don't see anything.

631
00:39:22,276 --> 00:39:24,403
I don't know if it will, but…

632
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:31,035
Utility poles have plates with
identification numbers written on them,

633
00:39:31,118 --> 00:39:33,621
which serve as the address
of the utility pole.

634
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:35,748
That's a huge clue.

635
00:39:35,831 --> 00:39:39,168
Lylea, please, tell us the truth.

636
00:39:40,086 --> 00:39:43,381
We will protect you and your family
with all our strength.

637
00:39:43,464 --> 00:39:46,967
Please, trust us.

638
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:54,517
Are you really going to protect me?

639
00:39:56,727 --> 00:39:57,978
Of course.

640
00:40:01,357 --> 00:40:02,650
That man…

641
00:40:04,527 --> 00:40:05,945
is not my husband.

642
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:09,407
The truth is…

643
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:36,517
Okay. Let us through.

644
00:40:44,442 --> 00:40:45,693
Wait.

645
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:48,195
We apologize,

646
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:50,114
but entry cannot be permitted.

647
00:40:50,197 --> 00:40:55,411
You are suspected of being involved
with a human trafficking organization.

648
00:40:56,787 --> 00:40:58,497
What the hell are you talking about? No.

649
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:01,459
Fukusawa, what's going on?

650
00:41:01,542 --> 00:41:04,920
We located the place
where your family was being confined.

651
00:41:23,647 --> 00:41:27,109
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

652
00:41:31,697 --> 00:41:34,241
-Entire family found.
-Clear!

653
00:41:34,783 --> 00:41:35,951
Don't move!

654
00:41:38,662 --> 00:41:39,997
Don't move!

655
00:41:41,582 --> 00:41:43,792
-What now?
-Hey!

656
00:41:43,876 --> 00:41:45,044
What was that?

657
00:41:46,462 --> 00:41:49,507
It wasn't me. It was not me.

658
00:41:49,590 --> 00:41:52,176
-Bring him up.
-Stand up.

659
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:57,389
Hideout suppressed. Family secured.

660
00:41:58,224 --> 00:41:59,266
Also…

661
00:42:00,935 --> 00:42:02,520
from the criminal group at the hideout,

662
00:42:02,603 --> 00:42:05,648
we obtained information on the broker,
who was the mastermind.

663
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:17,409
Lylea Sadikova. Or rather,
real name, Nadia Karimova.

664
00:42:25,125 --> 00:42:27,461
-Don't move!
-Stop!

665
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:29,964
-Stop!
-Don't touch me!

666
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:32,007
Stop resisting!

667
00:42:32,883 --> 00:42:34,051
We're borrowing a room.

668
00:42:35,135 --> 00:42:36,637
Let me go!

669
00:42:44,019 --> 00:42:45,729
My family? Are they safe?

670
00:42:45,813 --> 00:42:46,772
Yes.

671
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:48,816
It's okay now.

672
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:51,860
H-how?

673
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:57,825
Those dolls were giving
a signal asking for help.

674
00:42:58,492 --> 00:43:01,537
But there was one more signal.

675
00:43:07,710 --> 00:43:12,256
The zipper on this suitcase
has a structure that doesn't catch easily.

676
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:16,135
And yet, Samir…

677
00:43:27,229 --> 00:43:31,400
Mori said it caught her attention,
so we investigated.

678
00:43:39,825 --> 00:43:41,160
Take a look.

679
00:43:46,874 --> 00:43:48,500
The shape of his hand at this moment.

680
00:43:50,377 --> 00:43:51,712
A hand signal…

681
00:43:51,795 --> 00:43:54,256
-The same signal as those dolls.
-Yes.

682
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:59,219
An internationally known signal.
The meaning of this hand signal is

683
00:44:00,262 --> 00:44:01,764
-"help".
-"Help."

684
00:44:02,890 --> 00:44:06,894
The one asking for help was Samir.

685
00:44:09,563 --> 00:44:11,440
We also established contact with Zafaria.

686
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:14,610
This is your family.

687
00:44:14,693 --> 00:44:17,488
They were abducted by the organization
and brought to Japan, right?

688
00:44:17,571 --> 00:44:20,658
If anything happened to Lylea, the broker,

689
00:44:20,741 --> 00:44:22,201
your family would be in danger.

690
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:24,787
That's why you couldn't
tell anyone, right?

691
00:44:25,412 --> 00:44:26,330
But it's okay now.

692
00:44:32,294 --> 00:44:34,880
-Why didn't you tell us?
-I'm very sorry!

693
00:44:35,381 --> 00:44:37,841
You were trying
to persuade Lylea at the time.

694
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:40,761
Besides, when we tried to tell you,

695
00:44:40,844 --> 00:44:44,264
-Mori…
-Um…

696
00:44:44,848 --> 00:44:48,852
You got angry and said that
Customs should just stay out of it.

697
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:52,314
So if you knew that I,
from Customs, had spoken up,

698
00:44:52,398 --> 00:44:54,400
I was sure you'd be angry again.

699
00:44:55,442 --> 00:44:59,780
So we decided not to tell you.

700
00:45:03,158 --> 00:45:05,536
Are you angry after all?

701
00:45:07,162 --> 00:45:09,373
He's not angry. Right, Hayami?

702
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:12,167
Samir.

703
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:13,752
First, I apologize.

704
00:45:14,962 --> 00:45:18,298
We could not stop your family from being

705
00:45:18,382 --> 00:45:20,342
brought into this country at the border.

706
00:45:21,468 --> 00:45:22,928
So that the same thing
never happens again,

707
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:27,766
we will fulfill our duties
with even greater resolve.

708
00:45:31,854 --> 00:45:35,441
Your family is waiting.
Please go meet them.

709
00:45:51,206 --> 00:45:53,625
Welcome to Japan.

710
00:46:00,799 --> 00:46:02,885
Thank you.

711
00:46:55,187 --> 00:46:56,480
It really is far.

712
00:47:00,442 --> 00:47:01,485
Counselor.

713
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:04,780
Good work today.

714
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:11,286
Who on earth is that Machi Mori girl?

715
00:47:13,455 --> 00:47:16,542
Are you that frustrated
about being outsmarted?

716
00:47:17,918 --> 00:47:21,421
Well, she said it was
her first time in the field.

717
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:23,632
I wondered why such a rookie
was put on this team.

718
00:47:24,591 --> 00:47:25,551
Because I put her in.

719
00:47:27,135 --> 00:47:28,136
Just kidding.

720
00:47:28,804 --> 00:47:30,514
An interesting girl, isn't she?

721
00:47:31,306 --> 00:47:32,683
I'm looking forward to what's to come.

722
00:47:44,236 --> 00:47:45,988
Machi! Hey!

723
00:47:46,863 --> 00:47:48,240
Chika!

724
00:47:49,241 --> 00:47:50,993
Take a seat, please.

725
00:47:51,702 --> 00:47:54,413
That was quite a tough day, huh?

726
00:47:54,496 --> 00:47:55,706
Right?

727
00:47:55,789 --> 00:47:57,374
Here you go.

728
00:47:58,959 --> 00:48:01,628
What a cute girl.
Is she a friend of yours, Chika?

729
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:04,047
Yup. Eat up, Machi.

730
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:06,675
The inari sushi here is the best in Japan.

731
00:48:06,758 --> 00:48:07,884
She's exaggerating.

732
00:48:07,968 --> 00:48:10,804
But the love put into it
is number one in the world.

733
00:48:10,887 --> 00:48:12,514
Thank you for the meal.

734
00:48:13,849 --> 00:48:15,517
Man, I'm really glad

735
00:48:15,601 --> 00:48:18,270
to be working at the same airport as you.

736
00:48:26,194 --> 00:48:28,405
Hey, why are you in Customs
in the first place?

737
00:48:28,488 --> 00:48:30,240
You didn't say a word about that.

738
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:34,578
Because I like objects.

739
00:48:35,370 --> 00:48:36,747
I knew that much.

740
00:48:37,831 --> 00:48:39,249
And…

741
00:48:40,417 --> 00:48:41,501
Well, whatever.

742
00:48:42,919 --> 00:48:45,797
Here, eat up, eat up.

743
00:48:49,885 --> 00:48:52,804
-Oh my!
-Right?

744
00:48:52,888 --> 00:48:55,474
Hey, Ayako, she says it's great!

745
00:49:01,438 --> 00:49:03,607
MIDORI SUGIHARA
COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM

746
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:16,286
T-there's a bomb threat.

747
00:49:16,370 --> 00:49:19,706
<i>These 23 individuals</i>
<i>are subject to strict inspection.</i>

748
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:23,377
<i>Why was tonight's flight to Rome targeted?</i>

749
00:49:23,460 --> 00:49:25,379
<i>-It's almost time.</i>
-Wait, Machi!

750
00:49:25,462 --> 00:49:26,338
What are you doing?

751
00:49:26,421 --> 00:49:27,464
Get down!

752
00:49:28,173 --> 00:49:29,466
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
